llama.cpp (as fetched by Ollama v0.35.1, llama.cpp b11232, applied after
136): on gfx803, a prompt matmul that patch 106 sends through the fp32
SGEMM is computed over a token count rounded up to a multiple of 128, when
that adds at most a sixteenth. The results are the same bits.
gfx803-specific: engages only on 106's GCN4 path.

WHY
---
The base image's SGEMM shim runs its fastest fp32 tile (64x128, two
wavefronts) only on whole 128-column tiles, and a column count that is not
a multiple of 64 goes to an older tile. In a prompt matmul the columns are
the batch's tokens, so every batch but the full ones misses it: Ollama runs
a 2,800-token prompt as a 2,048- and a 752-token batch, and the 752 tokens
of Qwen3 8B ran at 256 tok/s against 2,048-token batches at their full rate.

WHAT
----
On 106's path the activations are already copied into padded rows; that
copy now gets the rounded-up column count with the extra columns zeroed,
the GEMM runs over all of them, and the product goes through 127's padded
output buffer, whose 2D copy keeps only the real columns. A batch is padded
only when that adds at most 1/16 of its columns (752 -> 768, 1,000 ->
1,024), so the extra work stays below what the faster tile gains. The
shim's tiles accumulate each output in the same order, so the real columns
are the same bits.

Result on an RX 590 (llama-bench, one batch of the given size, q8_0 KV
cache, flash attention, tok/s):

                          752 tokens         1000 tokens
    Qwen3 8B Q4_K_M    256.1 -> 267.3     245.4 -> 262.3
    Qwen3.5 9B         252.5 -> 266.7
    2048-token batches unchanged (no padding); Qwen3.6 35B-A3B's tail batch
    unchanged within noise (its prompt time is in the expert GEMM, 118)

Logits over 752-token batches (llama-perplexity -c 752 -b 752 -ub 752,
Qwen3.5 9B) are byte-identical with and without the patch.
test-backend-ops test -b ROCm0 -o MUL_MAT passes (1301/1301).

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -1512,11 +1512,23 @@
         src1_ptr = src1_alloc.get();
     }
 
+    // The image's SGEMM runs its fastest fp32 tile only on whole 128-column tiles and falls back to an
+    // older, slower tile for a column count that is not a multiple of 64, such as the 752-token tail of a
+    // 2800-token prompt in 2048-token batches. Where rounding the batch up to 128 columns adds at most a
+    // sixteenth, the product is computed over zero columns and the extra ones are dropped.
+    int64_t ne11_gemm = ne11;
     if (gcn4_to_fp32_ld != nullptr && ne11 > 1) {
+        const int64_t ne11_up = (ne11 + 127)/128*128;
+        if (ne11_up != ne11 && 16*(ne11_up - ne11) <= ne11) {
+            ne11_gemm = ne11_up;
+        }
         const int64_t ld = ne10 + 16;
-        src1_pad.alloc(ld*ne11);
+        src1_pad.alloc(ld*ne11_gemm);
         CUDA_CHECK(cudaMemcpy2DAsync(src1_pad.get(), ld*sizeof(cuda_t), src1_ptr, s11*sizeof(cuda_t), ne10*sizeof(cuda_t), ne11,
             cudaMemcpyDeviceToDevice, main_stream));
+        if (ne11_gemm != ne11) {
+            CUDA_CHECK(cudaMemsetAsync(src1_pad.get() + ld*ne11, 0, ld*(ne11_gemm - ne11)*sizeof(cuda_t), main_stream));
+        }
         src1_ptr = src1_pad.get();
         s11 = ld;
     }
@@ -1583,12 +1595,12 @@
     // apart. The product goes to padded columns and a 2D copy (0.65 ms) moves
     // it to dst.
     if (compute_type == GGML_TYPE_F32 && ne12 == 1 && ne13 == 1 && gcn4_to_fp32_ld != nullptr && ne11 > 1 &&
-            (ne0*sizeof(float)) % 32768 == 0) {
-        const int64_t ldd = ne0 + 16;
-        ggml_cuda_pool_alloc<float> gcn4_dst_pad(ctx.pool(), ldd*ne11);
+            ((ne0*sizeof(float)) % 32768 == 0 || ne11_gemm != ne11)) {
+        const int64_t ldd = (ne0*sizeof(float)) % 32768 == 0 ? ne0 + 16 : ne0;
+        ggml_cuda_pool_alloc<float> gcn4_dst_pad(ctx.pool(), ldd*ne11_gemm);
         CUBLAS_CHECK(
             cublasSgemm(cublas_h, CUBLAS_OP_T, CUBLAS_OP_N,
-                    ne01, ne11, ne10,
+                    ne01, ne11_gemm, ne10,
                     (const float *) alpha, (const float *) src0_ptr, s01,
                                            (const float *) src1_ptr, s11,
                     (const float *) beta,  gcn4_dst_pad.get(), ldd));
